2026-09-01T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Five items are out of compliance with the table (three certs, two missing gates). Followup task 18 covers bringing them into compliance.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2145) 'Exceptions this rule does not cover
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2145) '**Cross-signed certs during CA rotation.** RFD66606-2141's phases 2-3 mint a leaf that chains to both the old and new intermediate for the rotation window. That leaf's `notAfter` is whichever chain is shorter. The transition window is the specific case where two CAs overlap for a bounded time. Not covered here. RFD66606-2141 covers it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2145) '**External CAs.** Nothing this RFD says binds a certificate issued by Let's Encrypt, ZeroSSL, or a paid public CA. Those follow whatever their issuer says.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2145) '**Client certs used only by machine identity (workload).** SPIFFE- style short-lived (1 hour) X.509 SVIDs would sit under this row too if we adopted them. Today we do not, so the row is not in the table.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2145  1 LINE
 Text:Written

